From: lxcfs-admission-webhook maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] cpuview: make the cgroup hierarchy walk libc-agnostic

get_min_cpu_count_cfs() walks a cgroup path towards the root by calling
dirname() and then re-testing the *input* buffer, assuming dirname()
truncated it in place. POSIX does not require that: dirname() may return
a pointer to internal storage and leave its argument untouched.

musl does exactly that for single-component absolute paths --
dirname("/kubepods.slice") returns a static "/" and leaves
"/kubepods.slice" in the buffer -- so `while (strcmp(cur_sg, "/") != 0)`
never turns false. The FUSE worker thread servicing the read spins at
100% CPU inside the read callback and never answers the request, so
every reader of /proc/cpuinfo, /proc/stat and (with --enable-cfs)
/sys/devices/system/cpu/online wedges in uninterruptible sleep.

Copy dirname()'s result back into the buffer whenever it returned
separate storage, so the walk terminates on every libc.

Upstream report: https://github.com/lxc/lxcfs/issues/730
Introduced by:   https://github.com/lxc/lxcfs/pull/690 (first shipped in v7.0.0)

NOTE FOR MAINTAINERS: delete this patch (and the `patch` invocation in
lxcfs-image/Dockerfile) once upstream ships a release containing the
real fix. The build intentionally fails loudly if the patch no longer
applies, rather than silently publishing an image that can hang a node.
---
--- a/src/proc_cpuview.c
+++ b/src/proc_cpuview.c
@@ -495,6 +495,18 @@
 
 		char *parent = dirname(cur_sg); // walk up
 		if (strcmp(parent, ".") == 0) break; // in this case parent != cur_sg
+		/*
+		 * POSIX allows dirname() to return a pointer to internal
+		 * storage rather than truncating its argument in place.
+		 * musl does exactly that for a single-component absolute
+		 * path: dirname("/foo") hands back a static "/" and leaves
+		 * "/foo" untouched, so the loop condition below never turns
+		 * false and the FUSE worker thread spins forever at 100%
+		 * CPU. Copy the result back so the walk makes progress on
+		 * every libc. See https://github.com/lxc/lxcfs/issues/730
+		 */
+		if (parent != cur_sg)
+			memmove(cur_sg, parent, strlen(parent) + 1);
 	} while (strcmp(cur_sg, "/") != 0);
 	return got;
 }
